cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ast-pack in research or publications, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ast-pack: Tree-sitter call-graph slicing for minimal, syntactically valid LLM code context"
abstract: >-
  ast-pack parses a source repository (Python, TypeScript/TSX, JavaScript/JSX,
  Go, Rust) with Tree-sitter into a cross-file symbol and call graph. Starting
  from an entry point given as a symbol name, a file:line location or a raw
  stack trace, it walks callers and callees up to a configurable hop depth,
  adds the type definitions and constants that the reached code references,
  prunes all unrelated code into one-line markers, and emits a syntactically
  valid context bundle with exact file and line headers for large language
  models. On seven open-source repositories the bundles were 87-98.7% smaller
  than the full repositories, and 6,605 rendered files re-parsed without
  syntax errors.
